<p>Room Management takes care of all panels held in the conference rooms. The diversity of events taking place makes it necessary to maintain a lot of different materials, ranging from projectors to PA systems but also simpler things like office materials. Every event is different: you might be setting up a projector for a slideshow presentation, rearranging tables for a workshop, or troubleshooting something unexpected right before a panel starts. You can expect multiple short shifts of about 20-40 minutes throughout the day between events.</p>

<p>Fluency in English is mandatory for this position. You need to be reliable and will be expected to be on time. Technical knowledge is appreciated but not necessary. If you can plug in a cable and aren't afraid of buttons, you'll do just fine.</p>

<p>We provide manuals and process documentation for all positions. Experienced team members ("Council") and a Director on Duty are always available to help you during the convention.</p>

<p>While this ad is for Room Management, joining ConOps means you become part of the whole team. We encourage everyone to try different roles, you can pick your shifts across all our services using our self-scheduling tool. You're in control of your schedule. Pick the shifts that work for you, and we only step in if shifts still need filling. We expect around 4-5 hours per day you're at the convention, typically adding up to about 15-20 hours across the convention days (Wednesday to Saturday).</p>

<p>We ask our team members to arrive by Tuesday morning to help with setup and to be available on Sunday for teardown. Setup and teardown are an all-hands effort: regardless of your usual role, everyone pitches in. How much you contribute on those days is up to you, every pair of hands helps!</p>

<p>You must be a registered attendee of Eurofurence and meet the convention's minimum age requirement. No prior experience is needed. There is no application deadline, you can reach out to us at any time. We'll have a short, informal chat to get to know each other and figure out where you'd fit best.</p>

<h3>Why join ConOps?</h3>

<ul>
    <li>Help make this convention happen. Eurofurence is entirely volunteer-run!</li>
    <li>Look behind the scenes and have the opportunity to influence how things are done</li>
    <li>Access to the staff lounge (with slushies, soft ice, cup noodles, real food, and more)</li>
    <li>Our own ConOps back office with drinks, exclusive to the team</li>
    <li>A small token of appreciation for every team member each year</li>
    <li>A great team with great team spirit</li>
</ul>

<h3>Interested in joining Con Operations?</h3>

<p>A simple "Hi, I'm interested!" is enough to get started, a short introduction about yourself is also welcome. Please send us an email to <a href="mailto:ConOps@Eurofurence.org" target="_blank">ConOps@Eurofurence.org</a> or contact <a href="https://t.me/FurryTeddyBear" target="_blank">@FurryTeddyBear on Telegram</a>. Email is slightly preferred for initial contact; we usually continue the conversation on Telegram. While we strongly prefer applications before the convention, feel free to reach out to us if you're interested, even on short notice.</p>
